@title  PCSE00235 - title -> FIGHT -> VERSUS -> Solo Match -> three full matches, FIGHT AGAIN between them
@game   PCSE00235
@shot-every 300

# WHAT THIS RECIPE IS FOR
# ----------------------
# Rendering and frame-rate coverage of Dead or Alive 5 Plus GAMEPLAY: several whole matches,
# every round, the K.O./"YOU LOSE" screens, the post-match menu and fresh stages. The Vita runs
# DOA5+ fights at a locked 60 fps, so on a measured window from f3600 the expectation is 60
# presented frames a second at 100% speed.
#
# WHAT A RUN OF THIS LOOKS LIKE (2026-10-02, native headless, doafull1002c):
#   f000150-f001500  Tecmo Koei logo, the Team Ninja intro movie `ninja_vi.mp4`, Team Ninja logo
#   f001673          the autosave notice (sceMsgDialogInit) - the @wait anchor below
#   f001833-f003153  title, play style, main menu (times before the second hold was added) -> FIGHT -> VERSUS -> Solo Match, Kasumi vs
#                    Ayane, stage select (the versus-fight.recipe front end, 33 frames late)
#   f003600-f006300  match 1 (circus stage, "SHOW TIME"), lost; f6600 the post-match menu
#   f007000-f011700  match 2 (D.W.A. wrestling ring) after FIGHT AGAIN
#   f012000-f015600  match 3 (oil rig), and the post-match menu again at ~f15900
#
# HOW IT WAS AUTHORED
# - The boot HOLDS at 1640 until the title opens its autosave dialog (`@wait call
#   sceMsgDialogInit`: f1673 natively, later on a phone whose movie and loads take longer), so
#   every later input line runs late by the hold. The anchor must ARM BEFORE the call: at 1673
#   itself it armed in the frame the call was made, never saw it, and held input for ever.
# - The fight loop is FACE BUTTONS ONLY (triangle PUNCH, circle KICK, cross THROW, square HOLD,
#   triangle+circle), 120-frame cycles to the end. A direction in the loop moved the post-match
#   menu's cursor off FIGHT AGAIN and walked into the options pages for good (doafull1002);
#   with face buttons only, the CROSS in each cycle confirms FIGHT AGAIN (the default item) and
#   the run keeps fighting, whatever frame each match happens to end on.
# - A SECOND HOLD at 2000 waits for the main menu itself (`@wait call
#   sceAppUtilSystemParamGetString`, called once as it opens: f2054 natively). Without it the
#   phone's slower trip from the play-style dialog to the menu dropped the DOWN, and the CROSS
#   that followed opened STORY instead of FIGHT (phone job 521 played the story cutscenes).
#   The hold PULSES CROSS (a 2-frame tap every 60 held frames): on a phone the "Play style set
#   to casual" OK dialog opened AFTER the 1980 CROSS, and a silent hold for a menu that cannot
#   open until that dialog is answered waited for ever (phone job 533). No host call names the
#   dialog, so the hold answers whatever play-style screen is still up instead.
0: @section boot
1640: @wait call sceMsgDialogInit
1800: @section title
1800: start
1812:
1860: cross
1872:
1980: cross
1992:
2000: @wait call sceAppUtilSystemParamGetString pulse cross 60   # the main menu opens (f2054 native; later on a phone)
2100: @section main-menu
2100: down
2106:
2160: cross
2172:
2280: @section versus-solo-select
2280: cross
2292:
2400: cross
2412:
2520: cross
2532:
2640: cross
2652:
2760: cross
2772:
2880: cross
2892:
3000: cross
3012:
3120: @section stage-select
3120: cross
3132:
3300: @section fight
3400: @section fight-loop
